          {
            "url": "https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/240400/2/Defining%20national%20fossil%20fuel%20phase%20out%20roadmaps-%20a%20Colombian%20case%20study%20foreword.pdf",
            "title": "Defining National Fossil Fuel Phase Out Roadmaps",
            "snippet": "Title: Defining National Fossil Fuel Phase Out Roadmaps\n\nURL Source: https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/240400/2/Defining%20national%20fossil%20fuel%20phase%20out%20roadmaps-%20a%20Colombian%20case%20study%20foreword.pdf\n\nPublished Time: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 10:23:34 GMT\n\nNumber of Pages: 115\n\nMarkdown Content:\nDefining National Fossil \n\n# Fuel Phase Out Roadmaps \n\n## A Colombian Case Study \n\nAlejandro Romero Prieto, Elliott Johnson, Prof Steve Pye, Dan Zhang, \n\nProf Keywan Riahi, Dr Setu Pelz, Dr Shanta Barley, Prof Piers Forster \n\nApril 2026 Foreword by \n\n# Prof. Rachel Kyte \n\n# Special Representative \n\n# for Climate, UK \n\n# Government \n\n## The first summit on Transitioning \n\n## Away from Fossil Fuels (TAFF) \n\n## could not come at a more \n\n## important time. \n\nThe war in Iran is threatening fossil supplies \n\nglobally. Airports are running out of jet fuel and \n\nvital fertilizer shipments are being missed. The \n\nprice of diesel and petrol has risen sharply, \n\nthreatening livelihoods. Depending on fossil fuels \n\nto such an extent brings enormous risk – for \n\nsecurity, economies and the environment. \n\nThis roadmap for Colombia – a collaboration \n\nbetween Colombian and UK experts – shows a \n\nclear path to economic and societal benefit. It \n\nbuilds off examples of successful implementation \n\nof policies in other countries. For example, the UK \n\nclosed its last coal-fired power station last year. \n\nThe roadmaps show that investment is needed to \n\ndeliver change, but this investment brings rapid \n\nemission reduction and clear economic benefits \n\nby the 2030s. \n\nWe can learn from each other and the successes \n\naround the world. Climate councils such as \n\nthe UK Climate Change Committee and its \n\ncounterpart within the Colombian ministries have \n\nvery important roles to play",
